@nikwen 
Below are the test cases we used to reproduce this bug:
Electron version: 42.3.0
Electron Fiddle: 0.39.0
Operating system: Debian 10
CPU architecture: x64
Steps to reproduce:
Repeatedly click the button on the page to open the file selection dialog. After continuous operation for about 2 minutes, Fiddle will crash.
Sample code:
`<!DOCTYPE html>

<html lang="zh-CN">

<head>

    <meta charset="UTF-8">

    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>文件选择器 - 显示文件路径</title>

    <style>

        * {

            margin: 0;

            padding: 0;

            box-sizing: border-box;

            font-family: "Microsoft Yahei", sans-serif;

        }

        body {

            padding: 80px 20px;

            background-color: #f5f7fa;

            text-align: center;

        }

        .container {

            max-width: 600px;

            margin: 0 auto;

            background: #fff;

            padding: 40px 30px;

            border-radius: 12px;

            box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);

        }

        h2 {

            color: #333;

            margin-bottom: 30px;

        }

        #selectBtn {

            padding: 12px 32px;

            font-size: 16px;

            background-color: #1677ff;

            color: #fff;

            border: none;

            border-radius: 6px;

            cursor: pointer;

            transition: background 0.2s;

        }

        #selectBtn:hover {

            background-color: #4096ff;

        }

        .path-box {

            margin-top: 30px;

            padding: 16px;

            background: #f0f5ff;

            border-radius: 8px;

            text-align: left;

            word-break: break-all;

        }

        .tip {

            margin-top: 12px;

            font-size: 13px;

            color: #888;

        }

        /* 隐藏原生文件输入框 */

        #fileInput {

            display: none;

        }

    </style>

</head>

<body>

    <div class="container">

        <h2>点击按钮选择文件</h2>

        <!-- 隐藏原生文件input -->

        <input type="file" id="fileInput">

        <!-- 触发按钮 -->

        <button id="selectBtn">打开文件选择框</button>

        <!-- 展示文件路径区域 -->

        <div class="path-box" id="pathResult">

            选中文件后，文件名称/虚拟路径将显示在这里

        </div>

        <div class="tip">安全说明：浏览器出于安全策略，无法读取本地真实绝对路径，仅可获取文件名与虚拟路径</div>

    </div>



    <script>

        // 获取DOM元素

        const btn = document.getElementById('selectBtn');

        const fileInput = document.getElementById('fileInput');

        const resultBox = document.getElementById('pathResult');



        // 点击按钮触发文件选择框

        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {

            fileInput.click();

        });



        // 文件选中监听事件

        fileInput.addEventListener('change', (e) => {

            // 获取选中的文件列表

            const fileList = e.target.files;

            if (fileList.length === 0) {

                resultBox.innerText = "未选择任何文件";

                return;

            }

            // 获取第一个选中文件对象

            const targetFile = fileList[0];

            // 虚拟路径（浏览器返回的路径）

            const filePath = targetFile.webkitRelativePath || targetFile.name;



            // 打印到浏览器控制台

            console.log("选中文件路径：", filePath);

            // 页面展示路径

            resultBox.innerHTML = `

                <strong>文件虚拟路径/文件名：</strong><br>

                ${filePath}<br><br>

                <strong>文件名称：</strong>${targetFile.name}<br>

                <strong>文件大小：</strong>${(targetFile.size / 1024).toFixed(2)} KB

            `;

        });

    </script>

</body>

</html>`

### Description

If a `session.webRequest.onHeadersReceived` (or `onBeforeSendHeaders`) listener calls `callback()` with a `responseHeaders` / `requestHeaders` object containing an invalid name or value (e.g. a value with `\r\n` in it), the JS-to-`HttpResponseHeaders` conversion fails partway, but we ignore the converter's return value and apply the empty or partially-built set anyway. The net effect is that the response's original headers get replaced with whatever was converted before the bad entry, with no error surfaced to the app.

Relevant code: `WebRequest::OnHeadersReceivedListenerResult` and `WebRequest::OnBeforeSendHeadersListenerResult` in `shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_request.cc` both discard the `bool` from `gin::Converter<...>::FromV8`.

### Expected behavior

A conversion failure should throw back to the listener (or at minimum leave the original headers untouched and log), not swap in a half-built set.

### Actual behavior

Original headers are silently replaced by the partial override; headers listed after the invalid entry in the object never make it into the response.

### Testcase

```js
session.defaultSession.webRequest.onHeadersReceived((details, callback) => {
  callback({
    responseHeaders: {
      'X-Bad': ['oops\r\nX-Injected: 1'],
      ...details.responseHeaders
    }
  });
});
```

Load any page whose response carries an identifiable header and observe that header is gone.

